en or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le13ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wage gap "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the difference in salary between two groups of people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Almost everywhere, there is a wage gap between men and women."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you compare salaries between men and women."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to earn"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to work so that you receive payment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  A study has shown that female doctors earn an average of $12,000 less per year than men."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "counterpart"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person in a different category who has the same job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Female doctors earn less than their male counterparts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "patient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who requires medical treatment"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Female patients thought women doctors were friendlier and spent more time with them than male doctors."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scientific"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "based on science"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many scientific studies have found that women doctors spend more time with patients."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unfair"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not fair; not equal; not correct in principle"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This wage gap seems especially unfair because women doctors give better service than men doctors. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a finished action or event that is connected to the present in some way.  <br><bR> You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present perfect expresses an action that began in the past and has recently been finished or continues into the present. You use time markers like <span class=\"italic\">for, since and ever </span>with the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the past simple, the time is always past. You use time markers with the past like: <span class=\"italic\">then, ago, yesterday, when I was\u2026 </span>with the Simple Past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form the Present Perfect tense, you use <span class=\"strong\">have/has</span> + <span class=\"strong\">the past participle</span> of the base form of the verb."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Base Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Tense Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Past Participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"be\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"been\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" has been <br>have been \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"show\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"showed\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"shown\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" has shown <br>have shown\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"find\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" has found <br>have found\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"prove\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"proved\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"proven\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" has proven <br>have proven\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "A study has shown that female doctors earn an average of $12,000 less per year than their male counterparts. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Scientific studies have found that women doctors spend more time with patients than male doctors."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Expressing What is Necessary"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use certain expressions to talk about what is necessary to do in the future in order for something to happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>You have to...</li><li>You have got to\u2026 </li><li>I'm going to have to\u2026 </li><li>You need to\u2026</li>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Women have got to work longer hours to make the same salary as men."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Women doctors are going to have to try to reduce this gap. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Find a video on the Internet about the wage gap between women and men in different professional fields. Use the key words \u201cwage gap men women\u201d to find one.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Listen to the video."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take down as many notes as you can from the video."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to find out the difference between men's and women's salaries in different professions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the information to a partner or to the class."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I listen to a video on the wage gap."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I take notes about the wage gap."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the information."}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about jobs and work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about experiences that I have and haven't had."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about what is necessary. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " In general, do you think women earn less money than men? Why or why not?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In what fields does this happen?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct